      "generationMode": "built-in-imagegen",
      "selectionDate": "2026-08-02",
      "suggestedAlt": "A cat and dog resting peacefully together in a warm modern living room with natural side light.",
      "prompt": "Use case: photorealistic-natural\nAsset type: high-resolution wide website hero photography source for responsive desktop, miniapp, and social crops\nPrimary request: Create a premium but authentic lifestyle photograph of a real domestic cat and a real dog calmly resting together in a modern warm home.\nScene/backdrop: Quiet contemporary living room with natural side light, subtle pale wood grain, warm off-white woven fabric, and restrained small blue (#4A6CF7) and mint (#5BC8AF) decor accents. Everyday realism, uncluttered, safe after-care feeling.\nSubject: One anatomically correct real cat and one anatomically correct real dog, relaxed and peaceful, natural fur and posture, both fully visible enough to crop safely.\nStyle/medium: Photorealistic natural editorial lifestyle photography, candid rather than staged, realistic fur and fabric texture, restrained premium color grading, no glossy CGI look.\nComposition/framing: Extra-wide horizontal 16:9 composition. Keep the entire leftmost 40% completely clean as a quiet copy zone: only a softly lit plain warm off-white wall or extremely subtle unfocused neutral surface, with no pets, furniture edges, plants, decor, shadows, high-contrast lines, or objects. Place both animals and every meaningful scene detail entirely within the right 55%, with comfortable breathing room from the top, right, and bottom crop edges. Keep the central 5% as a gentle visual transition.\nLighting/mood: Soft natural side light, calm, reassuring, warm, trustworthy.\nText: none.\nConstraints: No people. Exactly one cat and one dog. Correct anatomy, natural paws and limbs, consistent light and reflections. The left copy zone must remain visually empty and low contrast. No key content near crop edges. Palette accents should be subtle, never saturated.\nAvoid: any text, letters, numbers, pseudo-text, interface, button, logo, brand mark, watermark, clinic, veterinary office, medical equipment, cage, kennel, cartoon, illustration, 3D render, duplicated animals, duplicated limbs, malformed paws, extra tails, inconsistent reflections, dramatic saturation or cinematic effects."
    },
    {
      "id": "hero.professional-care.source",
      "sourcePath": "hero/source/hero-professional-care-source-v1.png",
      "generationMode": "built-in-imagegen",
      "selectionDate": "2026-08-02",
      "suggestedAlt": "A cat beside a tidy home feeding station with fresh water, measured food, and a blank service-record device.",
      "prompt": "Use case: photorealistic-natural\nAsset type: high-resolution wide website hero photography source for responsive desktop, miniapp, and social crops\nPrimary request: Create an authentic, tidy home pet-care scene centered on a well-kept feeding station and a real cat nearby, suggesting reliable professional-quality daily care without looking clinical.\nScene/backdrop: Warm modern home dining or kitchen corner with pale wood and soft neutral plaster, a clean ceramic fresh-water bowl, a separate ceramic bowl holding a modest measured portion of dry food, and one plain phone-shaped service-record prop. The phone-shaped prop must have a dark blank unlit screen with absolutely no visible interface, icons, letters, numbers, or marks.\nSubject: Exactly one anatomically correct real cat, calm and attentive near the feeding station; natural posture and fur.\nStyle/medium: Photorealistic natural editorial home-care photography, candid and credible, real ceramic, wood, water, fur, and fabric textures, restrained premium color grading.\nComposition/framing: Extra-wide horizontal 16:9 composition. Place the cat, feeding bowls, measured food, fresh water, phone-shaped prop, and every meaningful object entirely within the left 55%, all with comfortable breathing room from the left, top, and bottom crop edges. Keep the entire rightmost 40% completely clean as a quiet copy zone: only a softly lit plain warm off-white wall or very subtle neutral blur, with no cat, furniture edges, bowls, props, plants, decor, shadows, high-contrast lines, or objects. Keep the central 5% as a gentle transition. Make the bowls and cat readable after responsive crops.\nLighting/mood: Natural morning window light, clean, reassuring, organized, warm but not orange.\nColor palette: Mostly warm neutrals with restrained small blue (#4A6CF7) and mint (#5BC8AF) accents; never strongly saturated.\nText: none.\nConstraints: No people. Correct cat anatomy, natural paws and tail, coherent perspective, consistent light and reflections. Right copy zone visually empty and low contrast. No key detail near crop edges. The blank phone-shaped prop is secondary and subtle.\nAvoid: any text, letters, numbers, pseudo-text, readable interface, icons, logo, brand mark, watermark, buttons, medical equipment, medicine, veterinary office, clinic, cage, kennel, cartoon, illustration, 3D render, duplicated cat, duplicated limbs, malformed paws, extra tail, floating objects, impossible bowl reflections, strong saturation, dramatic commercial effects."
    },
    {
      "id": "hero.community-companion.source",
      "sourcePath": "hero/source/hero-community-companion-source-v1.png",
      "generationMode": "built-in-imagegen-edit",
      "selectionDate": "2026-08-02",
      "suggestedAlt": "A cat and dog sharing a relaxed, affectionate moment in a warm sunlit living room.",
      "measuredRightmostAnimalPixelX": 1342,
      "measuredRightEdgeMarginPx": 329,
      "measuredRightEdgeMarginPercent": 19.7,
      "measurementMethod": "Original-resolution pixel-grid inspection with a conservative fur-inclusive boundary.",
      "prompt": "Use case: photorealistic-natural\nAsset type: second targeted composition correction to the provided Community Companion website Hero source\nInput image: Image 1 is the edit target. Preserve its compliant warm modern living-room scene, natural late-morning light, restrained blue/mint/amber palette, realistic editorial photography style, and clean left 40% copy zone.\nPrimary request: Change only the scale and horizontal position of the complete cat-and-dog group. Move the group meaningfully left and scale both animals uniformly to about 85% of their current size so the entire group occupies approximately 48% through 80% of the source width.\nHard measured boundary: For a 1672px-wide output, the rightmost visible animal pixel, including every strand of the dog's tail fur, must be at x <= 1420, leaving at least 252px (15% of width) of clear scene between the animals and the right canvas edge. This intentionally exceeds the required minimum 201px (12%) margin. No animal pixel may enter the leftmost 40%.\nAnatomy/framing: Keep exactly one real cat and one real dog. Preserve their relaxed pose and friendly expressions. Show both complete bodies, all paws, hindquarters, and both full tails. Do not crop, erase, duplicate, or deform any animal part. Keep visible floor beneath the animals and clear background/floor to their right.\nInvariants: Keep the leftmost 40% completely clean, object-free, and low contrast. Keep the same warm home theme and restrained palette. No people, text, pseudo-text, interface, logo, brand mark, watermark, medical equipment, clinic, cage, cartoon styling, or strong saturation.\nAvoid: any rightmost animal pixel beyond x=1420; less than 252px right breathing room; dog tail near the canvas edge; cat entering the copy zone; enlarged subjects; changed scene concept; duplicated limbs; malformed paws, tails, or bodies."
    }
